BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Ukulele for Beginners - Adult
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T140000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260714T150000
UID:69e12d11bd5c392c7644aadf@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Curious about the ukulele?   Join us for an introduction to
  this fun and easy to learn instrument.\nLearn chords\, strumming pattern
 s and simple songs.\nUkuleles provided.\nJust bring yourself and your love
  of music!\nSpace is limited\n.\nThis program is for\nadults only.
LOCATION:Richview\, Program Room B\, 2nd Floor
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/69e12d11bd5c392c7644aadf
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
SUMMARY:Wednesday Afternoon @ the Movies: The Unholy trinity
DTSTART;TZID=America/Toronto:20260429T130000
DTEND;TZID=America/Toronto:20260429T150000
UID:699b5c146724c63d00f468ae@tpl.bibliocommons.com
DESCRIPTION:Join us on Wednesday afternoon at the library for a screening 
 of the Unholy trinity movie.\nIn 1870s Montana\, Henry Broadway must aveng
 e his father's wrongful execution by killing the man who framed him. He he
 ads to the lawless town of Trinity\, where he's trapped between the sherif
 f\, Gabriel Dove (Pierce Brosnan)\, and the enigmatic St. Christopher (Sam
 uel L. Jackson). As secrets and danger unravel\, Henry fights to survive a
 nd uncover the truth in this high-stakes action-packed western.\nRated 14A
 . 1hr 35 mins.\nEnglish Subtitles for the Deaf and Hard of Hearing (SDH) w
 hen available.
LOCATION:Weston\, Program Room. Lower Level.
URL:https://tpl.bibliocommons.com/v2/events/699b5c146724c63d00f468ae
X-SOURCE:Toronto Public Library — Older Adults
END:VEVENT
